RISC OS system font, first version: YSFlight's own bitmap fonts.

The GUI draws all its text (FsGuiObject::defUnicodeRenderer) through
yssystemfont, so with the null back end the menus and dialogs were blank.
riscos/ysriscosbitmapsystemfont.cpp makes the same bitmaps as the X11
version (width rounded to 4; rows from the top, bottom first with reverse;
1, 16 or 32 bits per pixel) from ysbitmapfont's fixed-width fonts, chosen
by height. Latin-1 only (other characters are drawn as '?'). A FontManager
version, with the desktop's fonts, is planned.

For YSCE ysce_public 1b13297. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

